# What this file is for: keep generated build output out of the tree.
#
# notation/target/ is written by `cargo build` and `cargo test`. It is
# generated, it is large, and no reader of this program ever reads it --
# committing it would put thousands of machine-specific object files under
# version control and make every diff unreadable. The Rust lane builds the
# crate in place, so the directory appears without anyone deciding to make
# it; this rule is what stops it becoming tracked.
#
# Cargo.lock is NOT ignored and NOT tracked. This crate is a library
# (`notation/src/lib.rs`), so the lock file would pin the owner's toolchain
# rather than describe this program; it is regenerated by every build.
/notation/target/